# Homelab Notes: Private Self-Hosted Apps over Tailscale

Setup: Proxmox host, Nginx Proxy Manager (NPM) in an LXC container, Vaultwarden, a TrueNAS VM, Cloudflare DNS, and Tailscale.

Goal: reach the apps by domain name from my own devices only. No port forwarding, nothing exposed to the internet.

## How it works

- `*.example.com` resolves in Cloudflare to the NPM container's Tailscale address (100.x.x.x), DNS only.
- Only devices signed in to my tailnet can reach that address.
- NPM forwards each name to its backend on the home network.

```
Device (Tailscale on) -> 100.x.x.x (NPM container) -> NPM -> backend on 192.168.1.x
```

## Addresses

| Device | Address |
|---|---|
| Router/gateway | 192.168.1.254 |
| Proxmox host | 192.168.1.50 |
| NPM (container 101) | 192.168.1.80 and Tailscale 100.x.x.x |
| Vaultwarden (container 100) | 192.168.1.82 |
| TrueNAS (VM 104) | 192.168.1.88 |

## 1. Fix Proxmox network after moving (host console, as root)

```
nano /etc/network/interfaces
```

In the `vmbr0` section:

```
address 192.168.1.50/24
gateway 192.168.1.254
```

Update the host's own line in the hosts file (change only the IP):

```
nano /etc/hosts
reboot
```

Check addresses afterwards:

```
ip a
pct list
pct exec 100 ip a
pct exec 101 ip a
```

## 2. Give the NPM container Tailscale access (Proxmox host console)

Allow the TUN device in the container config:

```
nano /etc/pve/lxc/101.conf
```

Add at the bottom:

```
lxc.cgroup2.devices.allow: c 10:200 rwm
lxc.mount.entry: /dev/net/tun dev/net/tun none bind,create=file
```

Restart and install Tailscale inside the container:

```
pct reboot 101
pct enter 101
curl -fsSL https://tailscale.com/install.sh | sh
tailscale up
tailscale ip -4
exit
```

Open the login link from `tailscale up` and approve the device. `tailscale ip -4` prints the 100.x.x.x address.

From the host, add `--` before the command, or pct reads `-4` as its own option:

```
pct exec 101 -- tailscale ip -4
```

In the Tailscale admin console (Machines), open the container's menu and choose **Disable key expiry**.

## 3. Cloudflare DNS (DNS only, no proxy)

```
A      example.com   100.x.x.x     DNS only
CNAME  *             example.com   DNS only
```

The A record is the NPM container's Tailscale address. The wildcard follows it, so every subdomain resolves there. A proxied (orange cloud) record can't reach a private or Tailscale address, so keep both records grey.

## 4. Nginx Proxy Manager hosts

```
nginx.example.com    http://192.168.1.80:81
truenas.example.com  https://192.168.1.88:443
vault.example.com    https://192.168.1.82:8000
```

For HTTPS, request a Let's Encrypt certificate in NPM using the DNS Challenge with a Cloudflare API token (Zone > DNS > Edit). Keep the token out of this repo.

TrueNAS needs Websockets Support turned on.

## 5. Reserve DHCP addresses on the router

Reserve these so NPM's forward targets don't change:

```
192.168.1.80   NPM
192.168.1.82   Vaultwarden
192.168.1.88   TrueNAS
```

## 6. Testing

Browser (Tailscale on, Incognito window):

```
https://vault.example.com
https://truenas.example.com
https://nginx.example.com
```

All three at once in PowerShell:

```
foreach ($h in "vault","truenas","nginx") {
  $n = "$h.example.com"
  Write-Host "--- $n ---"
  nslookup $n 1.1.1.1 | Select-String "Address"
  curl.exe -k -s -o NUL -w "HTTP status: %{http_code}`n" https://$n
}
```

Each name should resolve to the 100.x.x.x address. A status of 200, 301, 302 or 307 means it works.

Backends directly:

```
curl.exe -k -s -o NUL -w "%{http_code}`n" https://192.168.1.82:8000
curl.exe -k -s -o NUL -w "%{http_code}`n" https://192.168.1.88
curl.exe -k -s -o NUL -w "%{http_code}`n" http://192.168.1.80:81
```

Phone:

1. Install Tailscale and sign in to the same account.
2. Turn Wi-Fi off, Tailscale on, then open the three URLs. They should load.
3. Turn Tailscale off and reload. They should fail, which confirms they are private.

## Direct addresses (no DNS needed, on the home network)

```
http://192.168.1.80:81
https://192.168.1.50:8006
https://192.168.1.82:8000
https://192.168.1.88
```

## Troubleshooting

- **Cloudflare returns its own IPs (104.x, 172.67.x):** the record is proxied. Set it to DNS only.
- **Router returns a name with no address:** the ISP gateway strips private (192.168.x) answers. Pointing DNS at the Tailscale 100.x address avoids this.
- **502 Bad Gateway:** NPM was reached but the forward IP, port or scheme is wrong. After moving networks, old 192.168.68.x addresses cause this.
- **504 or timeout:** Tailscale is off on the device, or the NPM container is offline in the Tailscale admin console.
- **Sites stop working after about 6 months:** the Tailscale key expired. Disable key expiry on the NPM container.
- **Phone fails:** turn off Private DNS (Android) or iCloud Private Relay and other VPNs (iPhone).
- **`pct exec` says "Unknown option":** add `--` before the command.
- Never expose the Proxmox UI (8006) or the NPM admin (81) to the internet.

## Never commit

Cloudflare API tokens, Tailscale auth keys, tunnel tokens, passwords, `.env` files, or exported NPM configs.
